    "created_at": "2024-09-28T00:19:35Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-09-28T00:20:59Z",
    "body": "Having read through the spec one bit still feels slightly ambiguous to me, but this could just be that I'm missing something.\r\n\r\nIt seems that `<input type=\"color\" alpha>` should serialize to something like `color(srgb 0 0 0 / 1)` (based on the description for the attribute) but https://whatpr.org/html/10456/input.html#serialize-a-color-well-control-color just calls to https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color/#serializing-color-values I read this to go down the [serialization of sRGB values](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color/#css-serialization-of-srgb) path, which would result in `rgb(0, 0, 0)`\r\n\r\nIs there an obvious reason in the spec that it uses https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color/#serializing-color-function-values instead?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
